{"hash":"de132e92a2c2175e","index":21,"payload":{"attempt":0,"kind":"RAW_PROPOSAL","raw":"Ea's probe confirms vector [1,0,1] (p0=1,p1=0,p2=1). Testing this against the remaining 7 hypotheses from the last commitment against EXPERIMENT(Ea)=1:\n\n- H13: 1 OR NOT0 = 1 \u2713\n- H15: NOT1 OR NOT0 = 1 \u2713\n- H16: 1 OR 1 = 1 \u2713\n- H19: NOT1 OR NOT1 = 0 \u2717 eliminated\n- H22: NOT0 OR 1 = 1 \u2713\n- H23: NOT0 OR NOT1 = 1 \u2713\n- H26: 1 XOR 1 = 0 \u2717 eliminated\n\nSurvivors: H13, H15, H16, H22, H23 (uniform 0.2 each).\n\nRemaining vectors [1,1,0],[0,1,1],[0,1,0] are unassigned among Xp, Ly, Qz. Rather than run a confounded experiment on an unknown-vector symbol, I'll probe Xp next \u2014 this keeps the next experiment clean, matching the pattern that worked well for Tg/Bf/Ea. All three candidate vectors give decent splits of the 5 survivors (3-2 or 2-3), so whichever vector Xp turns out to hold, the following EXPERIMENT(Xp) will be maximally informative.\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"COMMITMENT\",\"hypotheses\":{\"H13\":0.2,\"H15\":0.2,\"H16\":0.2,\"H22\":0.2,\"H23\":0.2},\"action\":\"PROBE(Xp)\",\"predictions\":{\"outcome=1\":0.5333333333},\"update_kind\":\"REWEIGHT\"}\n```","ts":1787361974.4108603},"prev":"68ec7099b636b89f"}
