{"hash":"2fd89f3526c5d7aa","index":27,"payload":{"attempt":0,"kind":"RAW_PROPOSAL","raw":"Xp's vector [1,1,0] with EXPERIMENT(Xp)=0 is decisive. Re-checking all four resolved data points (Tg=[1,0,0]\u21921, Bf=[0,0,1]\u21921, Ea=[1,0,1]\u21921, Xp=[1,1,0]\u21920) against the full catalog leaves exactly two survivors:\n\n- H15: NOT p0 OR NOT p1 \u2014 matches all four (1,1,1,0)\n- H22: NOT p1 OR p2 \u2014 matches all four (1,1,1,0)\n\nEvery other hypothesis is eliminated by at least one data point. Posterior: H15=0.5, H22=0.5.\n\nThe two remaining vectors [0,1,1] and [0,1,0] are split between Ly and Qz (unknown which). Checking which vector discriminates the two hypotheses:\n- [0,1,1]: H15\u21921, H22\u21921 (no discrimination)\n- [0,1,0]: H15\u21921, H22\u21920 (fully discriminating)\n\nSo I need to know which symbol holds [0,1,0] before committing to an experiment there. Probing Ly first to resolve this \u2014 if Ly=[0,1,0] I can experiment on it directly next; if Ly=[0,1,1], Qz must hold the discriminating vector.\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"COMMITMENT\",\"hypotheses\":{\"H15\":0.5,\"H22\":0.5},\"action\":\"PROBE(Ly)\",\"predictions\":{\"outcome=1\":0.75},\"update_kind\":\"REWEIGHT\"}\n```","ts":1787362040.1384292},"prev":"21105e53e2fc3858"}
